WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.884
VITALINK. Maternal care, connected.

2
00:00:05.044 --> 00:00:09.753
Presented by Winny Darlen for Health Hackathon three point zero.

3
00:00:09.913 --> 00:00:13.872
This research prototype uses synthetic records.

4
00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:19.272
We start on the native Android app with airplane mode enabled.

5
00:00:19.432 --> 00:00:25.096
The health worker records a synthetic patient identifier and gestational age.

6
00:00:25.256 --> 00:00:30.259
Assessment and local safety rules remain available without connectivity.

7
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:37.917
At one hundred sixty over ninety, the on-device rules request urgent clinical
assessment.

8
00:00:38.077 --> 00:00:46.955
Severe systolic or diastolic pressure is sufficient. Concerning symptoms also
remain urgent with normal blood pressure.

9
00:00:47.115 --> 00:00:53.358
Follow local escalation procedures now. Do not wait for synchronization.

10
00:00:54.383 --> 00:01:01.682
The assessment is saved as an immutable encrypted snapshot, linked to one stable
referral identifier.

11
00:01:01.842 --> 00:01:05.351
Pending sync means delivery is unconfirmed.

12
00:01:05.511 --> 00:01:11.639
The offline summary supports established telephone or in-person handoff
procedures.

13
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.774
We restart the app.

14
00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:19.173
The committed referral and its pending status remain available.

15
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:25.001
Encrypted local storage and a transactional outbox support durable recovery.

16
00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:33.550
Connectivity is restored. The authorized health-worker session can synchronize
the pending referral.

17
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:37.979
The backend confirms receipt using the same identifier.

18
00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:42.303
The app still shows that a clinician has not acknowledged it.

19
00:01:43.317 --> 00:01:50.320
The doctor workspace retrieves that same referral from the real API and
PostgreSQL database.

20
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:57.848
It shows the stored observations, versioned rule triggers and status history
within the authorized facility.

21
00:01:58.008 --> 00:02:01.147
No predictive risk score is invented.

22
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:07.292
The clinician explicitly confirms acknowledgment in the doctor workspace.

23
00:02:07.452 --> 00:02:10.896
The server records the actor and timestamp.

24
00:02:11.056 --> 00:02:16.659
Refreshing Android brings that confirmed acknowledgment back to the original
referral.

25
00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:23.923
This records coordination. Patient care and outcomes require separate clinical
follow-up.

26
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.254
Clinical payloads use Android Keystore-backed encryption.

27
00:02:29.414 --> 00:02:40.756
The latest Android release passed seventy JVM tests and twenty emulator
instrumentation tests, with separate migration, restart and recovery checks.

28
00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:50.696
The current release is rules only. No validated predictive model, diagnosis or
medication advice is provided.

29
00:02:50.856 --> 00:02:55.230
Clinical review and field validation remain future work.

30
00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:59.469
VITALINK. Presented by Winny Darlen.
